5.1. A Bayesian network for facial action unit modeling and recognition
\par
In recent years, a variety of approaches are proposed to recog-
\par
nize facial expressions. Besides recognizing six basic facial expres-
\par
sions directly, techniques have also been developed to automatically
\par
recognize facial action units. According to the Facial Action Unit Sys-
\par
tem (FACS) by Ekman [26], each AU is related to the contraction of
\par
a specific set of facial muscles. FACS has been demonstrated to be a
\par
powerful means for representing and characterizing a large number3054 W. Liao, Q. Ji / Pattern Recognition 42 (2009) 3046 -- 3056
