\par
from the queue and added to Iup if it is not in Iup. The parents
\par
of the node, if not present in Iup thus far, are added to the
\par
queue. The procedure terminates when the queue is empty.
\par
When it terminates, the set Iup becomes the upstream set. The
\par
procedure must terminate after a finite number of steps because
\par
an ID is a directed acyclic graph.
