\textbf{4 Design of Knowledge Representation}
\par
We present the design of our knowledge representation in five
\par
subsections: concepts and instances, three-tier representation of
\par
concepts, introduction of a basic design entity BDE , attributes of
\par
a BDE, and triplet expressions, relations, and transitivity.
\par
\textbf{4.1 Concept and Instance Levels. }Semantics and knowledge
\par
can be considered at two levels: 1 concept level, which describes
\par
the basic knowledge using concepts, relations, and axioms rel-
\par
evant to product design evaluations; and 2 instance level, which
\par
uses the concepts and instantiate them to associate the knowledge
\par
with the actual product data.
\par
Figure 2 shows these two levels and actual product data.
\par
