\par
amples are datum plane, datum axis, feature profile, etc. Thus, we
\par
extend the form attribute to describe any of the form attributes
\par
that are used during the design process. In other words, even those
\par
attributes which do not become part of the final design and are
\par
only used as intermediate information in the design process are
\par
built into the ontology. Examples include 2D profile and datum
\par
plane, which are used as auxiliary information during 3D feature
\par
creation.
